  "reserved": [
    {
      "english": "`pub` / `public` / `export`",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "publicus, 'public'",
      "role": "Marks a declaration as part of the module's interface. A `publica` function declares its `poscit` row explicitly (§4.1 rule 5), and public names must decompose under the lexicon (§3.1).",
      "word": "publica"
    },
    {
      "english": "`fn` / `function` / `def`",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "functio, 'a performance, a carrying out'",
      "role": "Declares a function. It also introduces function types, `functio(A) -> B poscit {R}`, and lambdas (§8.6).",
      "word": "functio"
    },
    {
      "english": "`struct`",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "structura, 'a putting together'",
      "role": "Declares a record type. A `structura` is always a value type with no implicit boxing (§6.3 decision 4); one with a capability-typed field is capability-bearing (§4.3).",
      "word": "structura"
    },
    {
      "english": "`type` / `enum`",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "typus, 'form, kind'",
      "role": "Declares a type: an alias, or a sum type written as comma-separated `casus` variants, as in `typus Color = casus ruber, casus viridis;` (§8.6).",
      "word": "typus"
    },
    {
      "english": "`interface` / `trait`",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "interfacies, 'outward appearance'",
      "role": "Declares an interface; `interfacies X in T poscit R { ... }` is an implementation. An interface's declared rows are a ceiling on every implementation (§4.4).",
      "word": "interfacies"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; a named set of capabilities",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "potestas, 'power, ability'",
      "role": "Names a set of capability atoms so a long `poscit` list is written once: `potestas Hospes = { alloc, ambitus }` (§4.5).",
      "word": "potestas"
    },
    {
      "english": "`extern` block / FFI",
      "group": "declaration",
      "latin": "externus, 'external'",
      "role": "Opens a foreign-function block with an explicit ABI, `externus(\"C\", abi: sysv_amd64) { ... }` (§5.3). A non-atomic `refero` may not cross it (`EXS-E0520`).",
      "word": "externus"
    },
    {
      "english": "`let` / `const` / `val`",
      "group": "binding",
      "latin": "firmus, 'firm, stable'",
      "role": "Binds an immutable name. Assigning to it is `EXS-E0306`. At module level it declares a constant (§8.6 decision 5).",
      "word": "firma"
    },
    {
      "english": "`let mut` / `var`",
      "group": "binding",
      "latin": "mutabilis, 'changeable'",
      "role": "Binds a reassignable variable. In type position it marks a mutable borrow, `&mutabilis T` (ADR 0016), the form a callee needs to write through a parameter.",
      "word": "mutabilis"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; closest to an effect or permission annotation",
      "group": "capability",
      "latin": "poscit, 'it requires' (indicative, describing)",
      "role": "Introduces a function's capability row, meaning authority drawn from the enclosing scope (§4.1 rule 4). It is bare on a declaration (`-> u8 poscit alloc, ambitus`) and braced in function and `dyn` types (`poscit { rete }`), and a lambda takes none.",
      "word": "poscit"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; a scoped dependency binding",
      "group": "capability",
      "latin": "sub, 'under'",
      "role": "Binds a capability provider for a scope: `sub ambitus = a;` to the end of the scope, or a block form (§4.5). The provider must have the atom's own capability type (`EXS-E0303` otherwise), and binding one atom twice in a scope is `EXS-E0422`.",
      "word": "sub"
    },
    {
      "english": "`as` (cast)",
      "group": "capability",
      "latin": "sicut, 'just as, in the way of'",
      "role": "Two uses: the cast `x sicut u32` (§8.6 level 3), and the row-substitution item `poscit sicut f`, meaning the row carried by parameter `f`'s type (§4.2). No `sicut` retypes a value into or out of a capability atom (`EXS-E0305`).",
      "word": "sicut"
    },
    {
      "english": "`dyn`",
      "group": "capability",
      "latin": "an English abbreviation of 'dynamic', the one non-Latin reserved word (§8.4)",
      "role": "Marks a trait object, `dyn Trait poscit {P}`, whose braced row narrows the trait's ceiling at the cast site (§4.4).",
      "word": "dyn"
    },
    {
      "english": "`return`",
      "group": "value flow",
      "latin": "reddere, imperative 'give back!'",
      "role": "Returns a value from a function, `redde expr;`, or `redde;` with none. It is an imperative, as `rumpe`, `perge`, `contrahe` and `discerne` are (§8.5, Mood).",
      "word": "redde"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; a placement suffix",
      "group": "value flow",
      "latin": "apud, 'at, beside'",
      "role": "Suffix in the type grammar for placement, `acies<f32, 1024> apud machina` (§8.6 Types), where a value lives; device placement is designed in §5.5.",
      "word": "apud"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; a reference-counted reference",
      "group": "value flow",
      "latin": "referre, 'to carry back' (refero, 'I carry back')",
      "role": "`refero<T>` is the non-atomic reference-counted reference type (§6.4). It cannot cross an `externus` boundary (`EXS-E0520`); `refero_communis<T>` is the atomic one and may. A bare `refero` with no `<T>` is `EXS-E0201`.",
      "word": "refero"
    },
    {
      "english": "`if`",
      "group": "condition",
      "latin": "si, 'if'",
      "role": "Opens a condition, `si COND { ... }`. The condition is an ordinary expression, so it needs no parentheses, and the body is always a braced block (§8.5).",
      "word": "si"
    },
    {
      "english": "`else if` / `elif`",
      "group": "condition",
      "latin": "sin, 'but if' (Cicero's correlative `si ... sin ...`)",
      "role": "The next test in a `si` ladder: `si x lt 0 { } sin x eq 0 { } aliter { }`. Latin supplies as one morpheme what other languages compound (§8.5).",
      "word": "sin"
    },
    {
      "english": "`else` / `default`",
      "group": "condition",
      "latin": "aliter, 'otherwise'",
      "role": "The final branch of a `si` ladder, and the catch-all arm of `discerne`: one word, one meaning, two places (§8.5).",
      "word": "aliter"
    },
    {
      "english": "`while`",
      "group": "iteration",
      "latin": "dum, 'while, as long as'",
      "role": "The sequential loop, written with a declared bound: `dum COND terminus N { ... }` (§8.5).",
      "word": "dum"
    },
    {
      "english": "`for`",
      "group": "iteration",
      "latin": "per, 'through'",
      "role": "The ordered loop, `per i in 0..n { ... }`: iteration k may observe iteration k-1 (§8.5).",
      "word": "per"
    },
    {
      "english": "none; a parallel for-each",
      "group": "iteration",
      "latin": "quisque, 'each one'",
      "role": "The independent loop, `quisque i in 0..n { ... }`: iterations do not observe one another and their order is unspecified. No dependency analysis exists, so today it is a trusted assertion `[OPEN]` (§8.5).",
      "word": "quisque"
    },
    {
